Z||000000||Pheagey||11-14-2001||09:49 PM||||   I have osme tires fomr an '87 Grand Am I want top put onto my '88 coupe ('cause someon stole my tires and I need wheels ASAP). Only thing is when I try to put them on they are about a 1/2" to small. Can I put lug nutes on 1st then the wheel then another set of lugs? It will only be like this for MAX 2 weeks (after I get my 1st paycheck from my 2nd job yada yada yada....).   Max speed:70, cruising:55-60.<BR>   thanks guys...<P>------------------<BR>'88 coupe, 5 speed.<BR>"The car formerly know as Dj's Fiero."||||reg||1
Z||000001||TRiAD||11-14-2001||10:53 PM||||If I understand this, you'd be using less than required lug nuts?<P>If that's right, than I only have one question for you...What is your butt worth to you? <P>Cynicism aside, your answer is <B>NO</B>. You cannot do that safely. <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0RAAAAN8VWdTblRDE93zkbJ*AbWuOFSwE0rtNS2h23KCe3aGgj1O!JDqud!IoFt1NPvdq6rh9ef*226xJh!nSf*vv2Id5gL8WoDCkDX*tCeM/1985-Signature-2.gif">    <BR><B><I><FONT COLOR="blue">Project MR1 ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</B> ~ Photoshop rendition of planned modifications</I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jake_Dragon||11-14-2001||10:56 PM||||You want to use a set of nuts to space your wheels out? sounds dangerous. if it was my car I would just wait.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Pheagey||11-15-2001||06:59 AM||||Triad, I'd be using double the number of lugs. One set as spaces (five per wheel) and another set to hold the wheel on (5 per wheel).<BR>And trust me i'd love to wait but I gatta get one of the two running by friday evening.||||reg||2
Z||000004||isthiswhereiputausername?||11-15-2001||07:39 AM||||I would say safely "no".   the wheel may just snap off soon as it gets to highway speed..     WHen a rim is bolted to the hub, its flush and the hub takes the weight, when you add spacers, you are putting the full force of the car on the spacer/lug ..   they arent that strong  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P><BR>Only other option would be to get wheel adaptors,  but it may be cheaper to get a few basic gm steel rims until you get money to buy a good set, <P> I know the wreckers charge $5-10 canadian a steel rim up here, <P>you might be able to get 4 rims and usable tires that will do until payday for around $50 if you look around..<P>I know its hard to do when its between paydays, but you could do more damage to your fiero or worse..<P><BR>Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000005||johnt671||11-15-2001||09:02 AM||||No way.  All the weight of the car would be on the lug studs and all of the forces from the road would be on the studs.  You would be very unsafe driving like this.  If the studs didn't just break the wheel would just flex and rip out around the lugs.  Like the suggestion above said get a cheap set of steel rims for now.  I have a set of the 14 inch aluminum wheels I'm not using, not in the best shape but they are straight.  I was going to keep them but I'd rather sell them than see you drive unsafe like that.  LMN||||reg||1
Z||000006||Pheagey||11-15-2001||09:03 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by isthiswhereiputausername?:<BR><B>...I know its hard to do when its between paydays, but you could do more damage to your fiero or worse..<BR>Good luck!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Like have (whats left) of my fiero junked?...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||JohnF||11-15-2001||09:24 AM||||Do not operate such a modified car.  We don't want to lose the Fiero!||||reg||1
Z||000008||Raydar||11-15-2001||09:51 AM||||Why do you see the need to do this?<BR>Are they rubbing on the back side of the wheels?<BR>Don't do your lugnut spacer method. Very dangerous, as outlined by previous posters.<BR>Doesn't Pep Boys sell aluminum spacers? That would be waaaaay safer. Be sure the studs are long enough to give the lugs enough threads for support. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||5
Z||000009||NEPTUNE||11-15-2001||10:24 AM||||PLEASE DONT KILL YOURSELF OR ANYONE ELSE!<BR>I have a set of good wheels and tires you can borrow till payday.they are from an 87. Can you pick up in south Orlando? <p>[This message has been edited by NEPTUNE (edited 11-15-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000010||AkursedX||11-15-2001||10:47 AM||||IF you decide to do this, I would suggest to at least use washers instead of lugnuts, I think that would be a little more sturdy.<P>I did this on my Plymouth Duster when I got winter tires and rims, but I only need a little clearance and I only used one thick washer on each lug.  It went fine all winter, but I would say that you would be taking your chances by going 1/2"||||reg||1
